From 7004345caffc0f80d970caab1456e24748a1be06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lunarthegrey <lunar@cypherpunk.is>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:39:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Edges: read UpCloud's load balancer plan list as the bare
 array it is

The UpCloud price read failed on every try with schema_mismatch: FCP
parsed `GET /1.3/load-balancer/plans` as `{ plans: [...] }`, but UpCloud
answers a bare JSON array (its API docs, and upcloud-go-api's
`[]LoadBalancerPlan` and recorded getloadbalancerplans.yaml). The
inventory swallowed the same mismatch, so the size picker had no plans.

- The plan list is read as a bare array, page by page (limit/offset,
  10 by default), keeping fields UpCloud adds. An answer that is not a
  list of named plans fails the read with `plan_list_unreadable`
  (counted as a provider fault, like schema_mismatch).
- The price list is read tolerantly: `prices.zone[]` by zone name, each
  item `{amount, price}` in cents an hour for `amount` units; other
  shapes of zone or item are skipped. A listed price's month is 672
  hours: UpCloud bills an hourly price for at most 28 days, as its own
  CLI prices a month (730 overstated it by ~8.6%).
- The plan's price key is still undocumented: every spelling of the
  product prefix is matched (with or without `plan_`). A plan the list
  does not name takes the dated table, one in neither has no known price
  without failing the read, and a warning names the zone's other item
  keys so the real key can be read from the logs.
- Fixtures in UpCloud's recorded shapes; wire contract gains the price
  read's calls; the location card words the price-read failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
